The main picture to remember
                    BEAN CONFIGURATION
                           |
             +-------------+-------------+
             |             |             |
            XML          Java        Annotations
             |             |             |
          <bean>     @Configuration    @Component
                        + @Bean           |
                                         |
                                  @ComponentScan

And this connects directly to what we discussed earlier:
@Component
    ↓
Class becomes a candidate for a Spring Bean

@ComponentScan
    ↓
Spring finds that class

Spring IoC Container
    ↓
Creates/manages the Bean

One subtle but important point: @Component by itself doesn't magically make Spring discover the class. The class needs to be
discovered through component scanning (which Spring Boot commonly configures automatically) or otherwise registered.





